{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.QuantumDilogarithmVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.QuantumDilogarithmVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.classical_limit_no_binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.classical_limit_no_binding","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean#L88-L93","doc":"At q = 1 (classical limit), ℏ_q = 0, reflecting that the\nclassical regime has no binding energy (degenerate configurations). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_qvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.beta_decay_qvalue","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean#L73-L86","doc":"The Q-value for beta decay is the difference in quantum\ndilogarithm volumes between parent and daughter, normalised\nby ℏ_q². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.quantum_dilogarithm_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.quantum_dilogarithm_volume","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean#L46-L71","doc":"**Quantum dilogarithm volume** (Proposition):\n\nThe nuclear binding energy equals the quantum dilogarithm volume\nof the Markov trace normalised by ℏ_q²:\n\n  E_bind(p, n) = Φ_q(N(Z, N)) / ℏ_q²\n\nAt q = 1, all crossings have equal weight, V̂ᵢ = 1,\nΦ_q = 0 (no binding).  At q > 1, crossing asymmetry\ncreates nonzero Φ_q and the nucleus is bound. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:quantum-dilogarithm-volume","label":"prop:quantum-dilogarithm-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bindingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bindingEnergy","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The nuclear binding energy from the quantum dilogarithm volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.quantumDilogarithmVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.quantumDilogarithmVolume","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean#L34-L40","doc":"The quantum dilogarithm volume of a nuclear link:\nΦ_q(N(Z,N)) = Σᵢ log|V̂ᵢ| = log Π|V̂ᵢ|.\n\nThis is the intensive volume, scaling as O(A) rather than\nO(e^A) for the raw Hecke weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean#L31-L32","doc":"The quantum Planck constant ℏ_q = (q - 1)/q. ","signatureChunk":0}]}